  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Conversion of a single dwelling house into a Large House in Multiple Occupation for 9 occupants(Sui Generis) & loft conversion incorporating a rear dormer.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a decent sized 3+ bedroom family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that there is an identified need, would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers, and would not be located in an area with a high level of access to public transport.&amp;nbsp; Additionally, the development site is not located within an area of high access to public transport and is therefore not considered an appropriate location for an HMO. &amp;nbsp; As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies: - National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)- Policies D6, D14 and T4 of the London Plan (March 2021)- Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to demonstrate that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area.&amp;nbsp; especially as the application site has a PTAL score of 3 indicating moderate access to public transport, and a bus stop and bus lane are immediately in front of the property thus no on-street parking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;. The proposal is therefore likely to exacerbate existing parking stress within the area thus add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site. &amp;nbsp;As such, it fails to comply with the following policies which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision:- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)- Policies T1, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)- Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
